      "title": "6. Practical Considerations in PID",
      "gist": "Using PID well requires matching redundancy measures to data type, gathering enough samples, choosing suitable software, and recognizing that the framework becomes intractable and uninterpretable for very large numbers of inputs.",
      "question": "practical PID use — what choices and limits must researchers navigate to apply this framework correctly? (tools and caveats)",
      "sourceHeading": "6. Practical Considerations in PID"
    },
