      "title": "6.3. Practical Limitations of the PID Framework",
      "gist": "The number of distinct information atoms explodes combinatorially with more input neurons, making full decomposition intractable beyond small groups, and like information measures PID suffers from biased entropy estimates in finite datasets.",
